WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.400
Let’s make a private lookbook for Maya,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.980
a bride at our sample
shop, Juniper Bridal.

00:00:05.937 --> 00:00:06.960
Start in the gown catalog.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.030
Vale is already selected.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.000
Click Faye to add a second gown.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.280
Both styles now appear
in Maya’s shortlist.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.800
Choose Build lookbook to set
the rules for her private link.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.530
Set the expiry to seven days.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.720
That gives Maya a week
to open her lookbook.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.880
Maya can try every gown as often as
she likes while her link is open.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.070
Your shop pays for delivered looks.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.245
In your shop workspace,
choose Send lookbook

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.020
to create the private link.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.080
Copy that link into a message to Maya

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.270
so she can open the gowns
you picked for her.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.290
Choose Copy invitation and
bride videos to include

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.710
the private lookbook and both
how-to videos in one message.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.920
Back in the demo, choose Open bride’s view

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:53.220
to see Maya’s side.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.570
Select Faye to see the
one-shoulder gown on Maya.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.440
On a live link, Maya
uploads a full-length photo,

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.160
enters her email, and gives
permission to generate her preview.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:08.610
She chooses See it on you
to generate her preview.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.220
The demo supplies a sample photo.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.610
Choose See reference photo
to see what she started with.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.870
Choose Show example try-on
to compare how the gown looks.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.390
If she wants to try it in person,

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.160
she chooses Request a fitting.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.430
Back in Fitting requests,
your stylist can see

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.440
Maya’s inquiry and email address.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.380
Use that address to agree
on an appointment time

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.640
and have her gown ready.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.980
Try the same steps in the demo.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.350
You can reset it and start
again with a different gown.
